 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+Staff ask the veterinarian directory's question in reverse: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A second page answers it, listing every specialty the clinic knows, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` (requested 2026-08-15). Every specialty appears under the name the clinic stores, and every veterinarian under a full name, first name before last. All specialties are shown together on one page rather than a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it, because the page lists specialties and not the whole roster. The page is reached by its own address; nothing else in the system links to it. Its own wording follows the language requirement, while stored specialty and veterinarian names are data rather than wording and are shown untranslated.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when `/specialties.html` is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the page is opened, then each holder is named first name before last.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the page is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the page is opened, then all of them appear together and nothing offers a further page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
